JACKSUM-MOD: Blake2bpDigest computes the remaining space of its buffer with 8 * BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES,
but the buffer is only PARALLELISM_DEGREE * BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES (4 * 128 = 512) bytes long.
Messages > 512 bytes that are fed in pieces cause an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException or a wrong hash value.
Upstream: still present in BC 1.73 .. 1.86 | Remove when: fixed upstream (patch no longer applies or is a no-op)

--- a/org/bouncycastle/crypto/digests/Blake2bpDigest.java
+++ b/org/bouncycastle/crypto/digests/Blake2bpDigest.java
@@ -63,7 +63,8 @@
     public void update(byte[] message, int offset, int len)
     {
         int left = bufferPos;
-        int remainingLength = 8*BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES - left;
+        // JACKSUM-MOD: the buffer is PARALLELISM_DEGREE * BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES (4 * 128) bytes long, not 8 * 128
+        int remainingLength = PARALLELISM_DEGREE*BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES - left;
 
         if(left != 0 && len >= remainingLength)
         {
